
---
title: Cuban Pork Roast
image: https://www.platingsandpairings.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/04/instant-pot-cuban-mojo-pork-10.jpg
cook time: 8 hour 20 minutes
nutrition:
  calories: 421 kcal
  fat: 13 g
  saturated fat: 3 g
  carbohydrates: 11 g
  sugar: 6 g
  protein: 60 g
  fiber: 1 g
  sodium: 1308 mg
  serving size: 1 serving
time required: 9 hour 30 minutes
servings: 6
cuisine: Cuban
source: https://www.platingsandpairings.com/instant-pot-cuban-mojo-pork-19
prep time: 10 minutes
course: Main Course
---

Combine @garlic{8%cloves} and @grapefruit juice{3/4%cup}(or one grapefruit, juiced), @lime{1}(zested and juiced), @olive oil{2%tbsp}, @brown sugar{2%tbsp}, @oregano{2%tsp}(or .5 tbsp fresh), @cumin{2%tsp}, and @kosher salt{1%tbsp} in a #food processor{}. Process until blended.

Add this mixture to a ziplock bag, along with @bay leaf{1} and @pork shoulder{3.5%pounds}(boneless, quartered). 

Let sit at room temperature ~{1%hour}, or refrigerated as long as overnight.

Place pork in a slow cooker and cook on low for 8 hours. 

Once the cooking time is up, remove the pork from the slow cooker. Season with @?salt{}(to taste). 

> Taste the cooking liquids for flavor. If bland, or watery, transfer to a pot on your stove, set over medium-high heat, and boil it down for 7-10 minutes. 

Shred the pork using two forks. Toss the shredded pork with about 1 cup of the cooking liquids.